-- title:
--   Ordinarity at odd p descends from the quotients A/𝔪^{m+1}
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a Noetherian commutative local ring and let $\rho$ be an object of [`GaloisRepAdic A`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16): a finite free $A$-module $V$ with $\operatorname{rank}_A V = 2$, together with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ (the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) to $\operatorname{End}_A V$ which is adically continuous, in the sense that for every $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak m^n\cdot V$ for all $v$. Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$. Assume that for every $m$ the base change of $\rho$ along the surjection $A \to A/\mathfrak m^{m+1}$ (a local homomorphism onto a nontrivial local ring) satisfies both: (i) `DetIsCyclotomic p`, i.e. the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal and, whenever $\sigma$ acts on the $p^n$-th roots of unity by $\mu \mapsto \mu^a$ with $a \in \mathbb{N}$, the determinant of $\rho(\sigma)$ is congruent to $a$ modulo the ideal generated by $p^n$; and (ii) `IsOrdinaryAt p`, i.e. for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $P$ there is a submodule $L$ spanned by the first member of some $A$-basis of the representation space indexed by `Fin 2`, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, and such that $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in L$ for all $v$ and all $\sigma$ in the image in the decomposition group of the inertia subgroup of $P$. The conclusion is that $\rho$ itself satisfies `IsOrdinaryAt p` over $A$.
--
--   This is the continuity (or Artinian approximation) part of the verification that ordinariness at an odd prime behaves like one of Mazur's axioms for a local deformation condition: the condition for a representation over a Noetherian local ring follows from the condition for all its Artinian truncations $A/\mathfrak m^{m+1}$, the determinant hypothesis supplying the $p$-distinguished inertia element used to pin down the line. It is used in the construction of the ordinary and strictly ordinary deformation conditions and in the comparison of the ordinary condition with flatness and with the residual representation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRepAdic_isOrdinaryAt_of_forall_quotient.lean

import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_LocalConditions

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem GaloisRepAdic.isOrdinaryAt_of_forall_quotient {A : Type} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] (ρ : GaloisRepAdic A) {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hp2 : p ≠ 2)
    (hdet : ∀ m : ℕ,
      haveI : Nontrivial (A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ (m + 1)) :=
        Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr (ne_top_of_le_ne_top
          (Ideal.IsMaximal.ne_top inferInstance) (Ideal.pow_le_self (Nat.succ_ne_zero m)))
      haveI : IsLocalRing (A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ (m + 1)) :=
        IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
      (ρ.baseChangeAlong (Ideal.Quotient.mk (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ (m + 1)))
          (IsLocalHom.of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective)).DetIsCyclotomic p)
    (h : ∀ m : ℕ,
      haveI : Nontrivial (A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ (m + 1)) :=
        Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr (ne_top_of_le_ne_top
          (Ideal.IsMaximal.ne_top inferInstance) (Ideal.pow_le_self (Nat.succ_ne_zero m)))
      haveI : IsLocalRing (A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ (m + 1)) :=
        IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
      (ρ.baseChangeAlong (Ideal.Quotient.mk (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ (m + 1)))
          (IsLocalHom.of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective)).IsOrdinaryAt p) :
    ρ.IsOrdinaryAt p := by sorry
